From: Project contributors <contributors@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] dae-wing: give new configs a default LAN interface

The dashboard creates its first config with lan_interface taken from the
interfaces that dae-wing flags as carrying a default route. That flag
checks route.Dst == nil, but netlink v1.3.1 reports default routes as
0.0.0.0/0 and ::/0, so no interface is ever flagged and the config is
created with no lan_interface. dae then binds only the WAN: the router's
own traffic is proxied while every forwarded LAN flow goes direct. On a
router the default-route interface would be the WAN anyway, not the LAN.

Fill an empty lan_interface of a newly created config from
DAED_DEFAULT_LAN_INTERFACE (comma or space separated), which the OpenWrt
init script sets from UCI. Updating a config is unchanged, so the
dashboard can still clear the list.
---
Index: daed-2.1.1/graphql/service/config/default_lan_test.go
